From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca C <clubdog123@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca808x: configure switch core memories in switch mode

In switch mode the QCA8386 switch-core memories must be handed over
explicitly, and the vendor requires it before UNIPHY1 is initialised.
Without it the switch core answers its hard-wired ID register but every
SRAM-backed register reads zero and writes are dropped.

Program MEM_CTRL/MEM_ACC for switch mode ahead of the uniphy bring-up.

Signed-off-by: Luca C <clubdog123@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca808x.c
@@ -154,6 +154,16 @@
 #define QCA8084_WORK_MODE_SWITCH		BIT(4)
 #define QCA8084_WORK_MODE_SWITCH_PORT4_SGMII	BIT(5)
 
+/* Switch-core memory configuration. In switch mode the core's memories have to
+ * be handed over explicitly before UNIPHY1 comes up; until then every
+ * SRAM-backed switch register reads back 0 and writes are dropped.
+ */
+#define QCA8084_MEM_CTRL_CFG			0xc90f044
+#define QCA8084_MEM_CTRL_DVS_MASK		GENMASK(9, 4)
+#define QCA8084_MEM_CTRL_DVS_SWITCH		BIT(5)
+#define QCA8084_MEM_ACC_CFG			0xc90f048
+#define QCA8084_MEM_ACC_SWITCH			0x000c0c0c
+
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Qualcomm Atheros QCA808X PHY driver");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("Matus Ujhelyi, Luo Jie");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
@@ -956,6 +966,24 @@ static int qca8084_phy_package_config_in
 	switch (shared_priv->package_mode) {
 	case QCA808X_PCS1_SGMII_MAC_PCS0_SGMII_MAC:
 	case QCA808X_PCS1_SGMII_MAC_PCS0_SGMII_PHY:
+		/* Hand the switch core its memories BEFORE UNIPHY1 is brought
+		 * up - the vendor SSDK has the same ordering requirement in
+		 * qca_mht_mem_ctrl_set(). Skipping this leaves the whole switch
+		 * core reading back zeros: the hard-wired ID register answers,
+		 * but PORT_STATUS/GLOBAL_FW_CTRL/PORT_LOOKUP never do, so no
+		 * frame can be forwarded.
+		 */
+		ret = qca8084_mii_modify(phydev, QCA8084_MEM_CTRL_CFG,
+					 QCA8084_MEM_CTRL_DVS_MASK,
+					 QCA8084_MEM_CTRL_DVS_SWITCH);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		ret = qca8084_mii_modify(phydev, QCA8084_MEM_ACC_CFG,
+					 U32_MAX, QCA8084_MEM_ACC_SWITCH);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
 		/* Switch mode: PCS1 runs SGMII+ towards the switch MAC0. There
 		 * is no xpcs node in this mode, so mdiodev[1] is NULL - do not
 		 * touch it here.
